        }
      ],
      "content": "an herb also called alecost (a composite plant (Balsamita vulgaris or Chrysanthemum balsamita) allied to Tansy, so called because formerly much used for giving to ale an agreeable aromatic and bitter flavor OED s.v. alecost) or costmary, an aromatic perennial plant, Chrysanthemum (Pyrethrum, Tanacetum) Balsamita, otherwise Balsamita vulgaris, family Compositæ, a native of the orient region, naturalized in the south of Europe, and cultivated in English gardens since the 16^th century as a flavoring herb; formerly used in medicine and to give a flavor to ale (OED s.v. costmary & cost n.^3)"
    }
